Pass -mno-incremental-linker-compatible only to Clang.

Lean adds the option on Windows so that Clang leaves out COFF timestamps.
GCC does not know it and stops with "unrecognized command-line option",
and the flags go to the compiler of every C file Lean builds, starting
with stage0's own library. Add it only when CMake's C compiler is Clang.
The stage0 snapshot carries the same rule, so it gets the same change.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments; changes nothing on CLANG64

--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -216,8 +216,8 @@
 string(APPEND LEAN_EXTRA_CXX_FLAGS " -ffp-contract=off")
 
 # On Windows we want to disable writing COFF object file time stamps.
-# LLVM 23 seems to have a regression in this regard.
-if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Windows")
+# LLVM 23 seems to have a regression in this regard. GCC has no such option.
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Windows" AND CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang")
   string(APPEND LEANC_EXTRA_CC_FLAGS " -mno-incremental-linker-compatible")
 endif()
 
--- a/stage0/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/stage0/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -216,8 +216,8 @@
